## 16. Definition of done / acceptance criteria

The task is complete only when all of the following are true:

- A native AirTon mobile app exists under `apps/mobile/` and starts successfully.
- The app has a cohesive, polished design system and functional navigation.
- Patient, clinician, and compact clinic/service demo personas are implemented.
- All key screens use deterministic, fictional fixtures and visibly declare simulation-only status.
- The measurement simulator can create accepted and rejected demo records, and rejected records never display an IOP number.
- OD and OS remain separate throughout history, charts, detail views, and reports.
- Every measurement exposes the required provenance and timestamp/clock metadata.
- Local-save, pending, delivered, and clinician-review states are visibly distinct and behave correctly.
- Offline simulation, duplicate retries, conflicting replays, review acknowledgements, and appended notes work in the demo.
- No real Bluetooth connection, physical actuator control, clinical inference, diagnosis, treatment guidance, cloud upload, or real authentication is falsely implied.
- Unconfigured care-plan, schedule, threshold, calibration, and retry parameters remain visibly unconfigured.
- The repository's current synthetic contract and safety invariants are covered by tests.
- TypeScript, lint, tests, Expo diagnostics, and Android debug build pass.
- A tagged release workflow can produce a consistently signed Android APK and AAB and publish them, plus checksums, as a GitHub Release when the required signing secrets are present.
- Existing Python and web CI checks remain intact.
- `apps/mobile/README.md` documents setup, run, test, build, demo roles, current limitations, release process, and required GitHub secrets.
- The final report lists changed files, commands run and results, produced artifact paths, CI workflow names, and remaining real-device/cloud/clinical integration gates. Never claim a test or release succeeded unless it was actually run and verified.

## 17. Final engineering principle

Optimize for trust, clarity, and traceability over feature count. A smaller app that faithfully distinguishes synthetic data, real device connectivity, acquisition quality, synchronization, and clinician review is much better than a visually impressive app that invents clinical certainty. Build the strongest possible mobile demonstration of the AirTon home-monitoring workflow while keeping every unverified hardware, ML, clinical, and cloud capability explicitly behind an interface and an honest “not yet available” state.